Task: Using data from both the regular season and the post-season, identify the pitcher who achieved the highest non-zero pitch speed for each team by confirming whether the pitcher’s ID appears in the relevant home or away player lists for that game, then retrieve that pitcher’s full name along with the maximum valid pitch speed they achieved while playing for that specific team.

Please think step by step and answer only one complete SQL in snowflake dialect in ```sql``` format.
SQL usage example: ```sql
SELECT "COLUMN_NAME" FROM DATABASE.SCHEMA.TABLE WHERE ... ``` (Adjust "DATABASE", "SCHEMA", and "TABLE" to match actual names, ensure all column names are enclosed in double quotations)
Here are some useful tips for answering:
When performing a UNION operation on many tables, ensure that all table names are explicitly listed. Union first and then add condition and selection. e.g. SELECT "col1", "col2" FROM (TABLE1 UNION ALL TABLE2) WHERE ...; Don't write sqls as (SELECT col1, col2 FROM TABLE1 WHERE ...) UNION ALL (SELECT col1, col2 FROM TABLE2 WHERE ...); Don't use ['-- Include all', '-- Omit', '-- Continue', '-- Union all', '-- ...', '-- List all', '-- Replace this', '-- Each table', '-- Add other'] to omit any table. Table names here: The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'BASEBALL': {'BASEBALL': ['BATTING', 'PLAYER']}}

When using ORDER BY xxx DESC, add NULLS LAST to exclude null records: ORDER BY xxx DESC NULLS LAST.
If the task description does not specify the number of decimal places, retain all decimals to four places.

[Self-refine]
2025-05-07 06:01:40 - Thread-292 (execute) - INFO - [Try to run SQL in self-refine]
```sql
/* ---------------------------------------------------------
   1)  Gather every pitch (regular-season + post-season)
       that has a valid (>0) recorded speed.
   2)  Attach the corresponding game so we know
       which club was HOME and which was AWAY.
   3)  Keep a pitch only when the pitcher’s ID really
       belongs to the side (home / away) he was pitching for
       in that particular game.
   4)  For each (team , pitcher) pair, keep the fastest
       pitch he ever threw for that club.
   5)  Per club, keep the single pitcher with the
       fastest (non-zero) pitch on record.
   6)  Bring in the PLAYER table to show the full name.
---------------------------------------------------------*/
WITH  all_pitches AS (            -- regular season  ∪  post-season
       SELECT  "GAME_ID",
               "PITCHER_ID",
               "PITCH_SPEED"::NUMBER  AS "PITCH_SPEED"
       FROM   (  SELECT "GAME_ID","PITCHER_ID","PITCH_SPEED"
                 FROM "BASEBALL"."BASEBALL"."PITCH_REGULAR"
                 UNION ALL
                 SELECT "GAME_ID","PITCHER_ID","PITCH_SPEED"
                 FROM "BASEBALL"."BASEBALL"."PITCH_POSTSEASON"
               )
       WHERE  "PITCH_SPEED"::NUMBER > 0
), 
games AS (
       SELECT "GAME_ID",
              "HOME_TEAM_ID",
              "AWAY_TEAM_ID",
              "HOME_PLAYER_IDS",      -- variant / ARRAY of player-ids
              "AWAY_PLAYER_IDS"
       FROM   "BASEBALL"."BASEBALL"."GAMES"
),
/* ---- pitches that truly belong to the HOME side -------- */
home_side AS (
       SELECT  p."PITCHER_ID",
               g."HOME_TEAM_ID"  AS "TEAM_ID",
               p."PITCH_SPEED"
       FROM   all_pitches p
       JOIN   games g
              ON p."GAME_ID" = g."GAME_ID"
       JOIN   LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => g."HOME_PLAYER_IDS") hp
              ON hp.VALUE::STRING = p."PITCHER_ID"
),
/* ---- pitches that truly belong to the AWAY side -------- */
away_side AS (
       SELECT  p."PITCHER_ID",
               g."AWAY_TEAM_ID"  AS "TEAM_ID",
               p."PITCH_SPEED"
       FROM   all_pitches p
       JOIN   games g
              ON p."GAME_ID" = g."GAME_ID"
       JOIN   LATERAL FLATTEN(INPUT => g."AWAY_PLAYER_IDS") ap
              ON ap.VALUE::STRING = p."PITCHER_ID"
),
/* ---- union of valid team-pitches ----------------------- */
team_pitches AS (
       SELECT * FROM home_side
       UNION ALL
       SELECT * FROM away_side
),
/* ---- fastest pitch per (team , pitcher) ---------------- */
max_pitch_per_pitcher AS (
       SELECT  "TEAM_ID",
               "PITCHER_ID",
               MAX("PITCH_SPEED") AS "MAX_SPEED"
       FROM    team_pitches
       GROUP BY "TEAM_ID","PITCHER_ID"
),
/* ---- rank pitchers inside each team by that max speed -- */
ranked AS (
       SELECT  "TEAM_ID",
               "PITCHER_ID",
               "MAX_SPEED",
               ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "TEAM_ID"
                                  ORDER BY "MAX_SPEED" DESC NULLS LAST) AS rn
       FROM    max_pitch_per_pitcher
)
/* ---- final answer -------------------------------------- */
SELECT  r."TEAM_ID",
        (pl."NAME_FIRST" || ' ' || pl."NAME_LAST")  AS "PITCHER_FULL_NAME",
        r."MAX_SPEED"
FROM    ranked r
JOIN    "BASEBALL"."BASEBALL"."PLAYER" pl
        ON pl."PLAYER_ID" = r."PITCHER_ID"
WHERE   r.rn = 1
ORDER BY r."TEAM_ID";
```
